  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Clan-head talk during the Awakening Ceremony names him the only rank five master of later generations and states he perished together with the Flower Wine Monk without leaving descendants.",
      "chapters": [
        4
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_awakening_ceremony",
        "char_flower_wine_monk"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Academy teaching places him as one of the clan’s two rank five masters, says he had remarkable talent and reached rank five, and tells the public story that he beat Flower Wine Monk, showed mercy, then died of wounds after a sneak attack while killing the Monk on the spot. Clansmen treat him as a great hero who sacrificed his life for the village.",
      "chapters": [
        7
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "That stage sits in the Gu Yue clan on Qing Mao Mountain.",
      "chapters": [
        4
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_yue_clan",
        "loc_qing_mao_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He wears the Gu Yue clan head uniform.",
      "chapters": [
        15
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gu_yue_bo"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Photo-audio Gu replay is suppressed truth: he tried to plot against Flower Wine Monk, lost the battle, then landed a sneak attack that only drove the Monk off, and surviving elders reversed those roles in the public clan story. Outside that recording, he eventually died from those fight consequences, and the Monk later died in the cave after Moonshadow Gu tainted him.",
      "chapters": [
        16
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "photo-audio-record",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_photo_audio_gu",
        "gu_moonshadow_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A later stretch states he possessed A grade aptitude, cultivated to rank five, and created another golden age for the clan, and that Flower Wine Monk achieved complete victory in their battle, killing him and downing a large majority of the elders while becoming infected by Moonshadow Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        163
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "spirit-spring-campaign",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "An earlier note after Moonshadow Gu’s effect is known still treats the sneak attack Gu as the one he used on Flower Wine Monk.",
      "chapters": [
        156
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "spirit-spring-campaign",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_sneak_attack_gu"
      ]
    }
  ],
